 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+The worker uses 2Q replacement so a sequential screening does not displace the repeatedly accessed comparison set. Replacement state consists of an incoming FIFO queue for previews seen once, a main LRU queue for previews seen more than once, and a bounded ghost FIFO containing keys for previews evicted from the incoming queue. The ghost queue contains no JPEG data and does not count toward the 12 GiB data limit.
+
+On a cache miss, a key absent from the ghost queue enters the incoming queue after rendering. A key found in the ghost queue is removed from the ghost queue and enters the main queue after rendering. A hit in the incoming queue promotes the entry to the most-recent end of the main queue; a hit in the main queue moves it to that queue's most-recent end. Concurrent requests still share one render job before any queue admission occurs.
+
+The incoming queue has a byte target within the 12 GiB budget; the main queue receives the remaining resident budget. When admission requires space, the worker evicts the oldest incoming entry while incoming data exceeds its target, recording the key in the ghost queue. Otherwise it evicts the least-recent main entry. If the selected queue is empty, it evicts from the other resident queue. The incoming target and ghost-queue bound are private worker settings that require initial values and workload tuning.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|-------------------------|-----------|
+| Cache replacement policy | 2Q | LRU; frequency-based eviction with aging | 2Q protects repeatedly reused comparison sheets from one-off sequential screening scans without changing the preview interface or render queue. Its additional private queues and tuning parameters are acceptable for that protection. |
